<title>EL SALVADOR: El Salvador coffee export update to Aug 15-Consejo.</title>
<headline>El Salvador coffee export update to Aug 15-Consejo.</headline>
<dateline>SAN SALVADOR 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salvadoran Coffee Council updated</p>
<p>coffee exports to Aug 15 for the 1996-1997 cycle.</p>
<p>Volumes in 100-lb (46-kg) bags, known as quintals.</p>
<p>    By Month		Quintals</p>
<p>    October			0</p>
<p>    November		58,125</p>
<p>    December		61,988</p>
<p>    January		490,088</p>
<p>    February	     376,800</p>
<p>    March		  421,913</p>
<p>    April		  639,888</p>
<p>    May		    364,020</p>
<p>    June		   214,104</p>
<p>    July		   189,594</p>
<p>    August		  *5,625</p>
<p>    September		 --</p>
<p>    Total		2,822,144</p>
<p>* Update to Aug 15</p>
<p>By Country</p>
<p>Europe</p>
<p>    Germany	    1,418,835</p>
<p>    Belgium		369,836</p>
<p>    Czech Rep.	     1,305</p>
<p>    Denmark		 12,750</p>
<p>    Spain		   41,520</p>
<p>    Finland		 11,250</p>
<p>    France		  82,125</p>
<p>    Netherlands	  164,262</p>
<p>    UK		     142,988</p>
<p>    Italy		   47,063</p>
<p>    Norway		   4,500</p>
<p>North America</p>
<p>    Canada		  50,025</p>
<p>    United States	421,757</p>
<p>Others</p>
<p>    Japan		   50,780</p>
<p>    Australia		1,125</p>
<p>    Morocco		  1,125</p>
<p>    S. Africa		  375</p>
<p>    Nicaragua		  900</p>
<p> Totals		  2,822,144</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
